// CLI strict-mode fixture for §10 row 12 of the type-hygiene PRD.
//
// Used by crates/reify-cli/tests/harness_cli/cli_type_hygiene_strict.rs to
// exercise the `--strict` exit-code split:
//
//   reify check type_hygiene_strict.ri          → exit 0 (Indeterminate is OK)
//   reify check --strict type_hygiene_strict.ri → exit non-zero (Strict fail)
//
// Why the constraint is INDETERMINATE (not Satisfied or Violated):
//   - `mass` is Undef because `divisor` is zero. The Undef comes from a
//     run-dependent value: change `divisor` and the constraint resolves.
//   - Bare-zero coercion still applies to `0` in `mass > 0`, giving it the
//     `Mass` dimension, but the LEFT operand `mass` is Undef.
//   - classify_undef sees the leaf cell as Undef → Indeterminate.
//
// This file must contain no `auto` param. A constraint that reads an Undef
// operand AND an auto makes the solve Infeasible (`comparison_residual` scores
// a non-numeric operand 1.0), which is an error that flips the exit code. An
// auto-free Undef is dropped from the solve, so the verdict here does not
// depend on whether the driver solves.
//
// Design choice (OCCT-independence):
//   Geometry-based indeterminacy (e.g. `constraint trace(moment_of_inertia(b,...)) > 0`)
//   would be SATISFIED under OCCT realization, making the strict-fail assertion
//   mode-dependent. An Undef scalar is Indeterminate on all runners and avoids
//   the OCCT-gating complication.
structure def TypeHygieneStrict {
    param divisor : Int = 0
    let mass : Mass = 1kg / divisor
    constraint mass > 0 && mass < 100kg
}
